From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tarwin Stroh-Spijer <tarwin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] h2: client: an empty SETTINGS from the server still migrates the request

A client connection that negotiates h2 via ALPN moves its original request
onto stream 1 when the server's first SETTINGS frame completes, in
lws_h2_parse_end_of_frame().  That only runs from frame_end, which a frame
reaches through its payload bytes, so a SETTINGS frame with no payload
never got there: the request was never migrated and never sent, and the
connection sat until its timeout.  An empty SETTINGS is valid (RFC 9113
6.5) and is what Node's http2 server sends by default.

Finish an empty non-ACK SETTINGS from the frame header parser instead.

Not yet upstream: main has the same code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
  lib/roles/h2/http2.c |    9 +++++++++
  1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/roles/h2/http2.c b/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
--- a/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
+++ b/lib/roles/h2/http2.c
@@ -1401,6 +1401,15 @@ lws_h2_parse_frame_header(struct lws *wsi)
 				lws_pps_schedule(wsi, pps);
 				wsi->h2_acked_settings = 1;
 			}
+
+			/*
+			 * An empty SETTINGS has no payload to reach frame_end
+			 * with, so finish it here: otherwise a client never
+			 * migrates its original request onto sid 1 and the
+			 * request is never sent
+			 */
+			if (!h2n->length && lws_h2_parse_end_of_frame(wsi))
+				return 1;
 			break;
 		}
 		/* came to us with ACK set... not allowed to have payload */
